	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "n0gcLsO8XCsa-pH-p",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 12, DX 14, IQ 4, HT 12, HP 12, WILL 7, PER 9, FP 12, SPEED 6.5, MOVE 24, DODGE 9, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nxcHmvNgRQEdeBAJH",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 32 (offense 28, protection 4), threat tier standard, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nptnvznPmS_8SHE1B",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/cheetah.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "n2n4JhbJJQQo0IUtr",
			"text": "Independent build total: 18 points of racial traits plus 16 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "nc8JLnZW2a_6N6N-N",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Cheetah (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "ni3R3mjjyUaEm4yW5",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "npHUoOgVnfCfdS1oK",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 6, 24 at a sprint (primary). The published Move folds this creature's Enhanced Move into a single figure."
		},
		{
			"id": "n8Gmt4t5pIAqXHpHO",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "nOczFG5XIGgY11i2s",
			"text": "Enhanced Move models the sprint. A cheetah that has run flat out is winded and disengages rather than fighting."
		},
		{
			"id": "nb2JLJ5D7C9eRvOcS",
			"text": "Rating caveat for review: the CER path credits Move linearly, so the sprint alone contributes 18 of this record's offense rating and lands it beside a lion. At the table a cheetah is much the lesser fight. Either the encounter weight or the sprint's accessibility should carry the correction; this build does not pre-empt that decision."
		},
		{
			"id": "np_BOO3bVrIaXj7uG",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
